  "caption": "Quinn had a grumpy heel, stiff mornings and a toe like a little sausage — plus psoriasis and changing nails.\n\nSkin and joints can be connected. Psoriatic arthritis can appear years after psoriasis. Stiffness that's worst after rest and eases with movement is a clue that it may not be just overuse.\n\nWhat can help: note your pattern, including morning stiffness over 30 minutes, ask your GP about a rheumatology opinion, photograph swollen fingers or toes, and keep up graded strength work, doing a lighter routine on flare days rather than stopping.\n\nGet same-day care for a painful red eye, and get checked for a hot swollen joint with fever or rapidly worsening swelling.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
